      <Desc>THE ORGANIZATION IS DEDICATED TO CARING FOR SURVIVORS OF TORTURE AND THEIR FAMILIES WHO LIVE IN SAN DIEGO COUNTY, HELPING THEM RECOVER FROM THEIR TRAUMAS THROUGH THE SUPPORT OF DEDICATED PROFESSIONALS AND COMMUNITY SUPPORTERS, INCLUDING MENTAL HEALTH, PSYCHIATRY, SOCIAL SERVICES, AND MEDICAL CASE MANAGEMENT. THE ORGANIZATION MAINTAINS A COORDINATED EFFORT AT THE LOCAL, STATE, AND NATIONAL GOVERNMENT LEVELS TO ADVOCATE ON BEHALF OF TORTURE SURVIVORS AND AGAINST THE USE OF TORTURE. THE ORGANIZATION CONTRIBUTES TO THE GOAL OF ENDING THE USE OF TORTURE THROUGH ADVOCACY AND EDUCATION.</Desc>
